# One-time setup for the one-click deploy script (scripts\deploy.ps1 /
# deploy.bat).
#
# Copy this file to the REPO ROOT (not scripts\) and rename it to
# ".env.deploy.local", then paste in the real PRODUCTION connection
# string from Vercel -> msp-crm project -> Settings -> Environment
# Variables -> DATABASE_URL (Production scope - NOT the Preview/Development
# one, and NOT whatever the Storage "quickstart" tab shows, which has been
# wrong before). See deployment-runbook.md for the full walkthrough.
#
# This file (.env.deploy.local, without ".example") is already covered by
# .gitignore's ".env*" pattern, so it will never be committed - but double
# check with "git status" after creating it if you want to be sure.
#
# deploy.ps1 only reads this as a FALLBACK, when $env:DATABASE_URL isn't
# already set in the PowerShell window it's running in. Having this file
# in place is what lets you just double-click deploy.bat and have the
# migration step work without typing anything except "YES" to confirm.

DATABASE_URL=paste-your-real-production-connection-string-here
